Following the review of the completed model identification templates, Clara and I identified a few points where the criteria have been applied inconsistently. We propose the following clarifications:

* Criterion II: clarify that simple arithmetic and mechanical aggregation do not constitute modelling techniques.
* Criterion III: clarify that deterministic processing does not imply absence of inherent uncertainty, as uncertainty may arise from the inputs, processing or outputs.
* Criterion V: remove it from the classification checklist and assess Model RTF scope separately. Alternatively, if retained, clarify that scope should be assessed based on the business use/risk type, irrespective of the tool’s current classification.

These clarify the application of the existing Model Risk Standard and do not change the underlying framework.

Unless anyone disagrees with this approach, I will apply it to the individual assessments and contact the relevant tool owners where updates are required.

